{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Maya. I'm happy to share my perspective as a forum participant. On what's working: the Thursday cadence is good, and having product, design, sales, and operations in the same room does create alignment opportunities. On what isn't: without a standing facilitator, meetings drift off-track and we lose time. Without a consistent way to submit concerns beforehand, people raise major issues mid-meeting with no context, and we can't make informed decisions. And with no required agenda lead time, there's no accountability for preparation. For concrete improvements, I'd suggest: first, appointing a standing facilitator — even on an interim basis — to keep meetings structured and time-boxed. Second, a shared intake doc where concerns must be logged at least 48 hours before each Thursday meeting. Third, a simple rule that any item not on the agenda by the cutoff gets deferred to the following week unless it's a genuine emergency. I do have something relevant to share about the facilitator role specifically — should I go into that now?"}
```

